Chapter: EffectLaunderMap
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils

 Adversarial probe (EffectRows.md stage 0). The canonical generic-HOF
 laundering route: an effectful function passed to list-map from a
 def declared pure. The application unify binds list-map's generic
 result variable to the argument's effectful type BEFORE the
 argument-boundary effect check compares them, so the check passes
 vacuously and the Console effect never surfaces in launder's
 signature. Declared-pure code performed I/O at runtime until effect
 rows stage 3b: list-map's row variable now carries the argument's
 Console effect into launder's ambient row, and the def boundary
 rejects it (CDX2031). This test is the enforcement's regression
 guard.

Section: Definitions

  shout : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  shout (n) = act
    print-line-uni ("shout " & show n)
    n * 2
  end

  launder : List Integer -> List Integer
  launder (xs) = list-map shout xs

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("len " & show (list-length (launder [1, 2, 3])))
  end
